045417] [17592186308371 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333073" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308371 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308371 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{2}(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308371 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "771c46b3-1f61-5283-9850-fe39ec331e05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308371 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)} &=L{4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)} &=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0) &=4L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0) &=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 &=4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2 &=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+(\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-3)+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-3s+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "69893fe7-9a8d-5f16-833d-a445576651e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308391 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186506606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186506621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186506630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186506652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186506656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186506621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505910 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "acf80487-30da-5578-b5d8-3413af242da3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506026 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506026 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506026 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "446d2e37-da3b-5ec4-9e85-ed0778e2a047" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506034 #edb/ref 1080 "-e^{2t}+1+3e^{4t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a5fa96f-7d32-5292-9419-4df3266355da" #edb/ref 175921